+
+    // Close the listening sockets this connection bound for its event and data ports. Nothing
+    // else closes them, so each connection would otherwise leave them listening for the life of
+    // the process. With the kernel choosing from tens of thousands of ports that goes unnoticed;
+    // with airplay_2_port_range set, the range fills up and the next SETUP can not bind a port.
+    // The event receiver thread, the only user of event_socket, has been cancelled and joined
